  </div>
  <div class="vp-body">
    <canvas id="lineage-canvas" style="width:100%;height:200px;display:block;"></canvas>
  </div>
</div>

<h3>Key Takeaways</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Static draft trees assume acceptance rates depend only on position, not context — this is demonstrably false</li>
  <li>Draft model confidence scores are a well-calibrated free proxy for target-model acceptance rates</li>
  <li>Path value V<sub>i</sub> (product of confidence along the path) is the right quantity to maximize</li>
  <li>Greedy selection of top-m nodes by V<sub>i</sub> provably maximizes expected accepted tokens</li>
  <li>20–40% speedup over static trees with zero additional training or architectural changes</li>
  <li>The intuition "branch when uncertain" is both correct and optimal — EAGLE-2 is the proof</li>
</ul>
</section>

